This is a dynamically quantized (QInt8 weights) build of an existing model,
and everything it derives from is Apache-2.0:

1. Laya
   https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya
   Copyright Convai Innovations and Laya contributors.

2. mizchi/laya-multilingual-onnx
   https://huggingface.co/mizchi/laya-multilingual-onnx
   The float16 ONNX export this was quantized from, itself produced by
   laya-mlx (https://github.com/mizchi/laya-mlx) from
   convaiinnovations/laya-multilingual (mmBERT-base, 322M parameters).

Changes made here (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)):
   - Cast the float16 initializers back to float32, dropped the graph's stale
     value_info shape hints, and applied onnxruntime's quantize_dynamic with
     QInt8 weights. 647 MB -> 325 MB.
   - Split model.onnx into four parts under GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit,
     with model.onnx.parts.json describing how to rejoin them.
   - Set "dtype": "int8" in onnx_config.json.

The tokenizer and the agent configuration are copied unchanged.
